WEBVTT

00:00:09.187 --> 00:00:10.427
Wow!

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.187
If this track could talk.

00:00:16.827 --> 00:00:20.227
Cruz, what do you say? Let's take a lap.

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:23.427
-(ENGINE REVVING)
-Oh, yeah!

00:00:28.507 --> 00:00:30.027
Oh, whoa!

00:00:43.707 --> 00:00:45.547
(CRUZ AND McQUEEN LAUGH)

00:00:46.387 --> 00:00:47.907
Yes! You nailed it!

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:49.747
Way easier without
the school bus of death

00:00:49.787 --> 00:00:50.827
trying to kill us! (LAUGHS)

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:52.267
Yeah, no kidding!

00:01:00.307 --> 00:01:01.627
(CHUCKLES AND GASPS)

00:01:02.027 --> 00:01:02.827
(YELLS)

00:01:03.787 --> 00:01:05.667
(GRUNTING)

00:01:09.147 --> 00:01:11.547
Was starting to think
I might never meet you.

00:01:12.427 --> 00:01:13.427
Smokey?

00:01:15.787 --> 00:01:16.747
(CRUZ GASPS)

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:19.267
He is alive.

00:01:19.947 --> 00:01:24.227
I know why you're here. You're thirsty.

00:01:24.947 --> 00:01:26.827
(COUNTRY MUSIC PLAYING FAINTLY)

00:01:28.507 --> 00:01:29.667
SMOKEY: I'll tell you what,

00:01:29.747 --> 00:01:32.547
these folks are gonna get a kick
out of meeting Hud's boy.

00:01:32.707 --> 00:01:37.307
Who's Hud? Oh, Doc Hudson! Right.

00:01:37.587 --> 00:01:39.387
(COUNTRY MUSIC PLAYING)

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:41.347
-Hey!
-(MUSIC STOPS)

00:01:41.987 --> 00:01:43.987
Act civilized. We got company.

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:47.067
Hey, Les.
How's that back axle treating you?

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:48.747
-Hey, sugar, welcome to Thomasville.
-(MUSIC CONTINUES)

00:01:49.627 --> 00:01:50.667
(McQUEEN CHUCKLES)

00:01:50.827 --> 00:01:53.227
-Would you look at that?
-CRUZ: What?

00:01:53.387 --> 00:01:55.627
McQUEEN: Three of the biggest
racing legends ever!

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:59.027
Junior "Midnight" Moon.
River Scott. Louise--

00:01:59.107 --> 00:02:01.507
Louise "Barnstormer" Nash?
She had 38 wins!

00:02:02.027 --> 00:02:05.187
Well, as I live and breathe.
If it ain't Lightning McQueen.

00:02:05.387 --> 00:02:07.387
Ms. Nash, it's a pleasure to meet you--

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:08.707
You've had a tough year, haven't you?

00:02:08.907 --> 00:02:09.987
Oh, uh...

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:12.867
Shouldn't you be running practice laps
in Florida by now?

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:15.627
-Yeah, sure, but--
-They're here to steal our secrets.

00:02:15.787 --> 00:02:17.427
Looking for your lost mojo?

00:02:17.907 --> 00:02:20.387
Wow. You don't mince words
around here, do you?

00:02:21.827 --> 00:02:23.627
(SCOFFS) Truth is always quicker, kid.

00:02:24.387 --> 00:02:25.907
(COUNTRY MUSIC PLAYING)

00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:32.427
♪ But all he kept talking about was

00:02:32.507 --> 00:02:34.147
♪ Glory days

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:38.507
♪ They'll pass you by Glory days

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:40.827
♪ In the wink of a young girl's eye

00:02:40.907 --> 00:02:42.347
♪ Glory days

00:02:42.507 --> 00:02:45.267
♪ Glory days ♪

00:02:45.427 --> 00:02:46.907
Guido, she's an angel.

00:02:46.987 --> 00:02:48.107
(ALL CHUCKLING)

00:02:48.227 --> 00:02:49.747
RIVER: Lou won't admit this,

00:02:49.827 --> 00:02:53.267
but she used to have
serious eyes for Hud.

00:02:53.867 --> 00:02:54.907
(CHUCKLES) Oh, really?

00:02:55.027 --> 00:02:56.827
Even if I did, it wouldn't have mattered.

00:02:56.987 --> 00:02:59.747
Hud didn't like fast women.
And that left me out.

00:02:59.787 --> 00:03:00.827
(LAUGHTER)

00:03:00.907 --> 00:03:03.547
Old Lou wasn't just fast,
she was fearless.

00:03:03.787 --> 00:03:06.867
The second I saw my first race,
I just knew I had to get in there.

00:03:07.027 --> 00:03:11.467
Of course, the fellas in charge
didn't like a lady racer showin' them up.

00:03:11.627 --> 00:03:13.187
So they wouldn't let me have a number.

00:03:13.427 --> 00:03:14.587
(GASPS) What did you do?

00:03:14.867 --> 00:03:16.107
I stole one!

00:03:16.307 --> 00:03:17.387
-What?
-Wow.

00:03:17.747 --> 00:03:20.547
Life's too short to take no
for an answer. Right, River?

00:03:20.707 --> 00:03:23.587
If we had waited for an invitation,
we might've never raced.

00:03:23.787 --> 00:03:26.187
And once we got on the track,
we didn't want to leave.

00:03:26.387 --> 00:03:27.987
I think that's how Doc felt too.

00:03:28.187 --> 00:03:30.267
You should've seen him
when he first came to town.

00:03:30.307 --> 00:03:32.147
Shiny blue paint.

00:03:32.307 --> 00:03:33.747
Not just the Hudson Hornet.

00:03:33.787 --> 00:03:35.627
He was already calling himself...

00:03:35.787 --> 00:03:37.947
ALL: ...the Fabulous Hudson Hornet.

00:03:38.027 --> 00:03:39.267
-Whoo-hoo!
-(ALL LAUGHING)

00:03:39.507 --> 00:03:41.387
Did we ever ride him on that.

00:03:41.547 --> 00:03:42.587
Not for long.

00:03:42.627 --> 00:03:45.507
Hud was the fastest racer
this side of the Mississippi.

00:03:45.787 --> 00:03:47.147
Until he wasn't.

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:48.627
What?

00:03:49.787 --> 00:03:52.147
Everything changed
when the rookie showed up.

00:03:52.747 --> 00:03:54.387
(ALL CHEERING)

00:03:58.707 --> 00:03:59.787
SMOKEY: Took Hud all of no time

00:04:00.027 --> 00:04:01.747
to work his way
through the best racers...

00:04:01.787 --> 00:04:03.387
in both Carolinas.

00:04:04.307 --> 00:04:08.147
Past River. Past Lou. Even Junior.

00:04:10.387 --> 00:04:12.347
But there was still
the rookie to deal with.

00:04:15.547 --> 00:04:17.227
Tried slamming him into the wall.

00:04:19.147 --> 00:04:21.907
But Hud never touched any wall,

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:23.147
unless he wanted to.

00:04:28.427 --> 00:04:29.827
(CROWD CHEERING)

00:04:34.187 --> 00:04:37.227
That rookie never saw
anything like that before.

00:04:37.387 --> 00:04:39.587
-Doc did that?
-Whoa! Are you kidding?

00:04:39.827 --> 00:04:42.947
Couldn't wipe the smile off his face
for a week after that.

00:04:43.307 --> 00:04:44.627
-(ALL LAUGH)
-(McQUEEN SIGHS)

00:04:44.947 --> 00:04:47.027
I wish I could've seen him like that.

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:51.067
-Like what?
-So happy.

00:04:58.227 --> 00:05:01.187
SMOKEY: You didn't come all this way
for a quart of oil, did you?

00:05:02.547 --> 00:05:04.427
I need your help, Smokey.

00:05:05.107 --> 00:05:07.587
Yeah? What kind of help?

00:05:08.907 --> 00:05:12.027
That's just it, I'm not sure.

00:05:12.107 --> 00:05:14.107
All I know is if I lose in Florida...

00:05:15.387 --> 00:05:17.107
it's over for me.

00:05:17.187 --> 00:05:19.387
What happened to Doc
will happen to me.

00:05:20.547 --> 00:05:22.227
What did happen to him?

00:05:23.547 --> 00:05:27.587
You know,
racing was the best part of his life.

00:05:27.787 --> 00:05:29.467
And when it ended, he--

00:05:30.827 --> 00:05:33.267
Well, we both know he was
never the same after that.

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:36.907
Is that what you think?

00:05:38.907 --> 00:05:41.587
Come on. I want to show you something.

00:05:47.587 --> 00:05:49.507
SMOKEY: You got the first part right.

00:05:50.147 --> 00:05:52.347
The crash broke Hud's body

00:05:52.427 --> 00:05:54.587
and the "no more racing"
broke his heart.

00:05:55.267 --> 00:05:56.627
He cut himself off.

00:05:56.707 --> 00:05:58.667
Disappeared to Radiator Springs.

00:05:58.827 --> 00:06:01.947
Son of a gun didn't talk to me
for 50 years.

00:06:02.587 --> 00:06:06.347
But then one day,
the letters started coming in.

00:06:18.907 --> 00:06:21.627
And every last one of them
was about you.

00:06:24.507 --> 00:06:27.587
Yeah, Hud loved racing.

00:06:28.627 --> 00:06:29.787
But coaching you?

00:06:30.747 --> 00:06:33.627
(SIGHS) I had never seen
the old grump so happy.

00:06:37.667 --> 00:06:40.627
Racing wasn't the best part of Hud's life.

00:06:42.147 --> 00:06:43.507
You were.

00:06:47.747 --> 00:06:49.347
You ready to blow out
a little carbon there, boy?

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:50.307
Yes, I am!

00:06:51.387 --> 00:06:52.467
(SCREAMS)

00:06:53.627 --> 00:06:55.867
You give it too much throttle,
you're in the tulips.

00:06:55.947 --> 00:06:56.947
(CHUCKLES)

00:06:57.667 --> 00:07:00.347
Hey, Lightning. You might want
to take notes on this one.

00:07:02.307 --> 00:07:03.307
(LAUGHS)

00:07:09.547 --> 00:07:10.787
(CHUCKLES)

00:07:12.987 --> 00:07:14.987
HUDSON: You got a lot of stuff, kid.

